WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.660
And in the book,

2
00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.360
I explain a concept that I call

3
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.120
the Cardinal Rule of Behavior Change,

4
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.440
which is that behaviors

5
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.100
that are immediately rewarded get repeated

6
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.600
and behaviors that are immediately punished

7
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.390
get avoided.

8
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.860
So you can think of pretty much any behavior

9
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.210
as producing multiple outcomes across time.

10
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.970
So for example, a bad habit, the outcome,

11
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.270
the immediate outcome is often positive.

12
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.880
So for example, you eat a donut

13
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.530
and right now it's tasty and sugary and enjoyable.

14
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.570
But the ultimate outcome is unfavorable.

15
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.540
You gain weight in two weeks

16
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:35.630
or a month or whatever.

17
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.170
For good habits, it's often the reverse.

18
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.230
Going to the gym right now,

19
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.190
the immediate outcome is a little bit unfavorable.

20
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.780
You sweat, it takes sacrifice,

21
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:45.950
you have to work hard,

22
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.690
you're panting and breathing hard.

23
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.090
But the ultimate outcome is favorable.

24
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.100
You get in shape

25
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.350
in two weeks or a month.

26
00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.100
And so much of the battle

27
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.380
of building good habits and breaking bad ones

28
00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:01.500
is about taking the punishments of your bad habits

29
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.220
and finding a way

30
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.990
to move those into the immediate moment

31
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.400
and taking the rewards of your good habits,

32
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.260
the ultimate outcome,

33
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.240
and finding a way

34
00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.030
to move that into the immediate moment.

35
00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.580
And I think

36
00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.190
when it comes to building good habits,

37
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.900
one of the best ways to do that

38
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.780
is to find an alternative way

39
00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.340
to be satisfied in the moment

40
00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:19.640
so that you're not waiting

41
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.790
for this long-term reward to show up.

42
00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:24.940
You know, like the reward

43
00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.520
for going to the gym for a month

44
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.770
isn't really a whole lot.

45
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.300
Like you don't really see

46
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.870
much of a change in your body.

47
00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:33.980
People probably aren't commenting

48
00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:35.190
on how you look different.

49
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.160
The weight on the scale

50
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.690
may not have changed that much.

51
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.620
So you need something more immediate

52
00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.190
to feel satisfied.

53
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.300
And that can either be

54
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.050
with an external reinforcement,

55
00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.060
like if I go to the gym

56
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.610
three days a week,

57
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.300
every week that I do that,

58
00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.920
then I get to take a bubble bath

59
00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.200
or I take a walk in the woods

60
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.000
or I get to watch my favorite TV show

61
00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.890
for an extra hour or something like that.
